cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use v2p in work you publish, please cite the repository and the
  exact commit you ran. There is no paper yet; when there is, this file
  will name it as the preferred citation.
title: "v2p: variant calls to protein sequences"
abstract: >-
  v2p converts genomic and transcriptomic variant calls into an amino-acid
  sequence database for mass-spectrometry search. It ingests somatic SNVs
  and indels, A-to-I RNA editing tables, gene fusion calls and
  alternative-splicing events into one database with a shared header
  vocabulary, and records a disposition for every input variant, including
  the ones that produce no protein.
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-07"
type: software

